On the daily chart $ETH has bounced nicely from the 2620 low and is now consolidating just above the short moving averages near 3000 but still well below the larger 99 day moving average around the mid 3800 region. This shows that the longer trend is still under repair while short term momentum has turned from bearish to neutral. Key support sits around 2900 and then 2620, while resistance levels to watch are near 3100 first and then 3300 where heavy supply may appear. As long as 2900 holds, pullbacks toward that zone can be used for gradual long entries, with a more aggressive bullish signal coming if price closes a daily candle above 3100 with rising volume.
