Next week, the global central bank showdown: will your Bitcoin rise or crash? Insiders are focused on Wednesday: once China's CPI is released, it will immediately decide whether to go all in or liquidate!

Hello everyone, I am Zitan. Next week, the global financial scene is going to explode with a bunch of major events piling up, and this is no small matter for our crypto market!

Look, the Federal Reserve, Australia, Switzerland, and Canada are all set to announce their interest rate decisions, not to mention China's CPI and social financing data for November.

Once these movements happen, capital flow will get chaotic, and Bitcoin, Ethereum, and others will have to shake three times.

Let me put it plainly: among these events, the Federal Reserve is the boss, and its interest rate decision is the most crucial. If the Fed takes a hawkish stance, hinting at interest rate hikes or tightening, the dollar will strengthen, and the appeal of crypto assets may decline, making the market prone to a drop;

Conversely, if it takes a dovish stance or the economic data is poor, global capital may flow into the crypto market for safety, giving us a chance to rise. So, retail investors need to stay alert; this is not the time to make money while lying down.

Specifically, day by day:

Monday: Japan and Germany data kick things off, but the impact is minimal;

Tuesday: Watch the U.S. inflation expectations for direction;

Wednesday: The most exciting day, as China's CPI and social financing data are released, reflecting the state of China's economy. If the data looks bad, global sentiment may collapse, and crypto might sneakily rise;

Thursday: Australia's unemployment rate and U.S. unemployment claims data may stir short-term volatility;

Friday: European data will wrap things up. Overall, keep a close eye on Wednesday and Thursday, as the Fed's decision is around the corner. Once there are any hints, the market will change its face immediately.

What impact will this have on the crypto market? Simply put, if interest rates rise, funds may flow out of the crypto space; if economic data is poor, the crypto space may become a safe haven.

What should retail investors do? Don’t panic! If you have a heavy position, you can reduce some holdings in advance to hedge against risks; if you’re bold, wait for bad data and buy a little at the bottom, hoping for a rebound. But remember, don’t go all in; the market can change its face faster than flipping a page.

